    <section>
        <h3>About Me</h3>

        <p>
            My name is Thomas Hunt and I am a year 11 at Sacred Heart College.
            I have 3 brothers and 1 sister who are extremely annoying, especially my sister.
            I did some sports that include basketball, waka ama and my favourite, rowing.
            I started doing rowing at year 10 and I wasn't the greatest at first when it comes
            to pulling watts, but as I move forward I started to get better at this sport and
            made a lot of friends on the way. I also do a lot of coding in my free time since
            I am aiming to become a software engineer in the future. I like gaming as well, games
            like Minecraft, Fortnite and Roblox pretty much lower my stress level. Although, when
            it comes to no internet situations, I play some nostalgic offline mobile games like
            Subway Surfers and Plants vs Zombies. I also sometimes like to draw, specifically drawing
            stickman poses where I mostly draw combat poses and its pretty cool. 
        </p>
    </section>

    <article>
        <h2>My Time at Sacred Heart College</h2>

        <p>
            I started at Sacred Heart College in Year 9, and during this time, I lived in the
            school hostel. While I met a few people who were kind and friendly towards me, there
            were also some students who acted strangely and sometimes said things that made me
            feel uncomfortable. Academically, Mathematics was one of my stronger subjects, while
            Science was probably my weakest. However, there were still certain topics in Science
            that I found interesting. Year 9 was also the year I first started Waka Ama, which
            quickly became a sport I really enjoyed. One of the highlights was competing in a
            regatta at Ian Show Park with my friends. We performed really well and came first
            in our race, earning gold medals. It was a memorable experience and one of the
            moments that made my first year at Sacred Heart special.
        </p>

        <p>
            Year 10 was a year of improvement and new experiences for me. Compared to Year 9,
            I worked harder on my schoolwork and managed to improve my grades across my subjects.
            One subject that I particularly enjoyed was Computer Science, where I achieved some
            good grades and developed a strong interest in programming and technology. Because
            of this, Computer Science became my favourite subject and made me consider it as
            something I might want to pursue in the future. Outside of academics, I decided to
            quit Waka Ama and started playing basketball instead, which gave me the opportunity
            to try a different sport and meet new people. However, the biggest change for me was starting rowing. At first, I was not the
            strongest rower and struggled with some parts of the sport, but as I continued
            training, I began to improve. I quickly fell in love with rowing because I enjoyed
            the challenge, the teamwork, and the feeling of getting better over time.
        </p>
    </article>

